nodes.goal:
Close out the scratch lane honestly. Scratch parent: {run.baseline_dir}; the copy path is DETERMINISTIC: {run.baseline_dir}/{run.issue_id} - no record lookup needed, which matters because on the halt-at-intake arm the baseline node was pruned and you must still run. If neither halt-notice nor a publish/hold record is in your inputs (## Inputs), the run died mid-lane: keep the copy, report kept=true and say what you found on disk.
Rules: if the publish record says published=true, remove the scratch copy (rm -rf its exact validated path - confirm it is under the scratch parent first, same escape law as creation) so no stale half-fix lingers as a working directory someone might trust. If publication did NOT happen (halted or held), KEEP the copy and say so - the committed fix lives there. Verify after removing: the path is gone AND the original project checkout ({run.project_dir}) still has no scratch remnants inside it (the lane was always a sibling/child of the scratch parent, never inside the repo).
Reply with ONLY fenced json {"cleaned": true|false, "kept": true|false, "removal_checked": "<what you ran and saw>", "note": "<state of the fix: pushed|held|none>"}
